Pantheon Operator

You may already have Semantic Zoom.

This feels slightly different.

I’d define something like:

Oscillator

Continuously vary the level of abstraction while preserving invariants.

Its job is

* detect over-generalization
* detect over-specialization
* identify the scale where a phenomenon becomes simplest
* move fluidly when new evidence appears

⸻

Why this matters

Many disagreements happen because people are operating at different resolutions.

For example:

* A psychologist explains behavior through cognition.
* An economist through incentives.
* A biologist through evolution.
* A sociologist through institutions.

Often they aren’t contradicting each other. They’re observing the same phenomenon at different scales.

The Pantheon could explicitly represent that by treating scale as a navigable dimension rather than a fixed commitment.

⸻

I think this also refines your earlier Metafold idea.

A Metafold changes the geometry of the conceptual space.

An Oscillation changes your position and resolution within or across that geometry while preserving the invariant you’re tracking.

One redesign I’d consider is making resolution a first-class coordinate attached to every concept and translation. Then every operator—partition, factorization, compression, translation, or Metafold—could declare the scales at which it is most informative. That would make “zooming” an explicit capability of the Pantheon rather than an informal habit.